    "text": "A wire of density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> is stretched between two clamps&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> apart. The resulting strain in the wire is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The lowest frequency of the transverse vibrations in the wire (Young&#39;s modulus of wire&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Nm</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ), (to the nearest integer),_______",
